        "original_id": "9155f78a-d47d-5a23-8251-8a60298aa23c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Thom Yorke, Bruce Guthro\n- Bands: Radiohead, Runrig, Films of Colour\n- Songs: \"All I Need\"\n- Places: Cape Breton Island, Nova Scotia\n- Topics: music roles, band membership, song themes, musical comparisons\n\nFacts:\n- Thom Yorke was born on 7 October 1968.\n- Bruce Guthro was born as Bruce Guthrie on 31 August 1961.\n- Bruce Guthro is a Canadian singer-songwriter from Cape Breton Island, Nova Scotia.\n- Thom Yorke is an English musician and composer best known as the singer and principal songwriter of Radiohead.\n- In 1998, Bruce Guthro joined the Scottish folk rock band Runrig while continuing his solo career.\n- Bruce Guthro has also recorded as a solo artist.\n- \"All I Need\" is a Radiohead song described as one of the band's most direct love songs.\n- In \"All I Need,\" Thom Yorke sings about obsession and unrequited love over a downbeat track.\n- Films of Colour's sound was compared to Radiohead, Muse, Coldplay, early Bloc Party, and Miike Snow.",
